hamin: And if you ever start packing, I get forty minutes' notice. I know how fast you are.
you: I'm not packing.
hamin[smile]: I know. I'd have noticed. {p}It's just nice to have it in writing.
> Your phone buzzes against the step.
> *I want to sit here until the cans are empty.* And, a second later: *That was today's. I'm not doing another one till tomorrow.*
> You finish your drink in six sips. He watches you do it and says nothing, and looks deeply content to have been right.
> You have always left in spring. In spring, this year, somebody will be counting. It is a strange, solid thing to know. Like a wall you can put your back against.
@show daniel smile at=l
daniel: Hamin. {{playerName}}. We've voted. It's the kimbap place. Songha made a ballot.
hamin: How many cups?
daniel: What?
hamin[smile]: Order nine of everything. I'm counting from there.
@hide daniel
> He gets up, and holds out a hand to pull you to your feet, and you take it, and that's all it is, and it's plenty.
> Behind you, on the laundromat step, two empty cans stand side by side in the first of the sun. Not lost. Just finished.
> Through the glass, the song reaches its key change. He hums it. So do you. Neither of you lands it.
@ending hamin_beside
@credits
@end

=== hamin_ending_someday
@bg studio_lobby t=fade d=1.2
@music echo
@amb room
@fx memory n=0.6
@time 04:58
@show hamin neutral at=c
> He hears it. You watch the two words land, and go down through six years of him like a stone through clear water.
hamin: Next time.
you: Next time.
hamin[thinking]: I know what I meant when I said that. I was fourteen. I meant "please come back."
hamin: What do you mean?
you: I mean I'm coming back. And I'm in no hurry. Those are the same thing, for once.
> He breathes out. Something in his shoulders that has been braced since midnight, waiting to be asked for an answer right now, lets go.
hamin[smile]: …Okay. {p}Good. I'm slow. I was hoping that was allowed.
@textbox echo
echo: RECORD 02 — OWNER: HAMIN. SELECTED FOR PRESERVATION.
echo: Contents: four minutes and twelve seconds of sea. One laugh. One name, resolved.
echo: One phrase: "next time". I have held it as unresolved for six years. I am not resolving it. I am handing it over.
echo: Please look after it. It has been very patient.
@textbox normal
@sfx chime
> On the desk, a small square of glass fills with light, as the tide fills a footprint.
@show hyunjun smile at=r
hyunjun: "Next time." That's "one more stop" with better manners. I support it completely.
@show haruta smile at=l
haruta: It's a good cut. You end on the promise, not the arrival. People remember those longer.
hamin: It isn't a cut.
haruta: No. {p}It's the bit where you know there's a sequel.
@hide all
@show justin smile at=l
justin: Do I still get to do the sea choreography?
@show hamin smile at=c
hamin: In July.
justin[neutral]: Why July?
hamin: I don't know yet. I've just decided it's July.
@hide all
@call echo_farewell
@bg dawn_river t=slow d=2.4
@time 05:40
@music hamin
@amb birds
@fx light n=0.5
@cam wide
> It takes eleven minutes to walk from Studio 25 to the river. He knows the way from anywhere.
> The path is empty. A long grey sheet of water with pink coming up under it. One early cyclist, far off, going the other way.
@show hamin neutral at=c
> You stop at the railing. He puts himself on the side the wind's coming from. You notice. You let him, this once, and make a note to take the next one.
hamin: I should say it properly. Out loud. I've been saying it with cans all night.
hamin: It's not a big deal, but— {p}no. It's a big deal.
hamin[neutral]: I like you. {p}Not as weather. Not as a cup. I like you. I checked it twice, and it held both times.
you: I like you too. I checked it once. I didn't need the second time.
> He laughs, the open one, head down, and the river takes it and doesn't give it back.
hamin: Then can I say the other thing? It's going to sound like the opposite. It isn't.
you: Say it.
hamin[thinking]: I've had one night of someone asking what I want. I'm not good at it yet. I said "egg sandwich" like it was a confession.
hamin: I don't want to hand you someone who's still working out how to have a preference.
hamin: I want to get better at it. And I want you to be there while I do. Not waiting. Just there.
* [sincere] "I've never stayed anywhere long enough for something to arrive slowly. I want to find out what that's like."
    hamin: Slowly.
    you: I've done fast. Fast is forty minutes and a box. I want the other one.
    hamin[smile]: …Then we want the same thing. I've never been able to say that sentence before.
* [playful] "Good. I've only just unpacked the kettle. One thing at a time."
    hamin[smile]: The kettle comes first.
    you: The kettle's load-bearing.
    hamin: I respect that. {p}I'll be second. I'm a very good second. I'll work my way up.
* [quiet] Move round to the windward side of him, so the wind reaches you first instead.
    > He starts to protest. Then he understands what you're saying, and stops.
    hamin[smile]: …You're going to keep doing that.
    you: For as long as it takes. That's the point.
> He takes something out of his pocket. The roll of masking tape from the lost property box. The marker. Of course he kept them.
hamin: I want it labelled. So it isn't just a feeling in a box.
> He tears off a strip, presses it to the railing, and writes. Small square capitals. He isn't hiding this one with his arm.
> JULY. BUSAN. THE BEACH BY THE SEAWALL. 23:41.
hamin: That's when the recording starts. I'd like to start the next one at the same minute.
hamin: Ten months. It's a long time. It isn't a test. I'll see you tomorrow, and on Tuesday, and I'll still know your order.
hamin: But on that beach, at that minute, I'd like to say "stay a bit" first. Before the can. As someone who's had some practice.
you: What do I bring?
> He writes a second line under the first.
@if var.drink == "peach"
    > BRING: ONE PEACH ICED TEA. ONE CORN TEA. A COAT, BECAUSE YOU WON'T.
@elif var.drink == "choco"
    > BRING: ONE HOT CHOCOLATE, IF IT'S NOT SOLD OUT. ONE CORN TEA. A COAT, BECAUSE YOU WON'T.
@elif var.drink == "coffee"
    > BRING: ONE BLACK COFFEE. ONE CORN TEA. A COAT, BECAUSE YOU WON'T.
@else
    > BRING: ONE GRAPE SODA. ONE CORN TEA. A COAT, BECAUSE YOU WON'T.
hamin: I'll buy them. You just have to be shivering thirty metres down the beach. For accuracy.
you: And you'll walk past me to the machine.
hamin[smile]: And then I'll come back. {p}That's the part I'm changing.
> He peels the label off the railing, carefully, so it doesn't tear, and sticks it to the back of your phone. He presses the edges flat with his thumb.
hamin: NOT LOST. I ran out of room to write it. It's implied.
> You have always left in spring. July is on the far side of spring. You will have to stay through the whole of it to get there, and you find that you've already decided to.
you: It's louder in the morning. The river.
hamin: It's the same.
hamin: Everything else is just waking up.
> His shoulder is next to yours on the railing. Not touching. Close enough that it's a promise and not a question.
> Below you, the river goes on towards the sea, the long way round, in no hurry at all. It gets there every time.
@ending hamin_someday
@credits
@end
